n  Nation against heteromorphs also known  as people with mutant type quirks May  hint at a connection between this  important issue and the last great  mystery yet to be revealed in the story  who is deku's Father and where has he  been all this time just to recap a  little bit in the middle of the Epic  final fight between Deku and shigaraki  the manga suddenly shifted gears and yes  pun intended instead of focusing on the  big main fights that are currently  taking place including the shigaraki  fight the all-for-one fight and the  Dobby fight mha chose to give us some  really dark and serious World building  as the discrimination against mutant  type Quirk users was finally explored in  detail with the help of meso Shoji and  his personal life experience the  Discrimination of mutant type Quirk  users has been hinted at before so this  is not completely new to us but  realistically we should have gotten more  information about this sooner Shoji  turned out to be such a fascinating and  inspirational character with a tragic  and compelling backstory and yet we  hardly knew anything about him until the  very last stages of the story that is  kind of a shame in my opinion before  this Shoji was always just kind of a  background character in class 1a and yet  he has so much to offer and so we  learned that even though in big cities  there is more equality and heteromorphs  hold some important positions of power  discrimination is still alive and well  in the countryside and it's showing no  signs of going away the villains who are  currently attacking the hospital believe  that all mutants type Quirk users who  side with the heroes and the hero  Society are spoiled City Slickers who  don't know what their fellow  heteromorphs are going through outside  the big city the previous chapter ended  with Shoji and Koda fighting the  villains to protect the innocent people  at the hospital despite being mutant  type Quirk users themselves and despite  the fact that Shoji is no City Slicker  he actually comes from the country side  and he went through a lot of hardship  and discrimination as others attacked  him as a child for having quote unquote  tainted blood the latest chapter picks  up as Shoji asks spinner whether he's  even considered the safety of the  innocent civilians at the hospital  before he decided to launch this  dangerous attack Shoji also adds that if  the answer is no he will never forgive  spinner and his cronies and this makes  sense to be honest since there are very  likely some innocent heteromorphs at the  hospital as well this means that even if  we accepted the claims of the villains  that they are fighting for the rights  and freedoms of mutant Quirk users their  own actions are not even consistent with  that claim they are actively endangering  fellow heteromorphs as much as every  other person in the area that they're  attacking so who are they really  protecting who are they really fighting  for Shoji's question is a good one and  the other heteromorphs who have been  supporting spinner are now beginning to  pay attention to the conversation they  also noticed that Shoji has some serious  scars on his face scars that make it  clear that he's gone through a lot and  he's not just some pampered City kid the  crowd tells spinner to explain the  righteousness of their cause to Shoji  but spinner has no idea what's going on  and he can't even begin to coherently  answer the question he just looks like a  drugged out Godzilla and the only words  that he can produce are no idea the  crowd is confused by this and the  Paranormal Liberation Front Commander  from the previous chapter tries to save  the situation by claiming that spinner  is saying that normal people have no  idea how much the mutant Quirk users  have suffered this seems to be enough  for the crowd for now but Shoji persists  he tells spinner that this attack is  going to set their cause back by 30  years since innocent people are about to  get hurt 