s also willfully  covering up the fact that spinner is not  all there and that the real leader  behind this movement is actually all for  one I am highly suspicious of this  Commander guy he doesn't seem to be  genuinely interested in his own cause  he's more of a propagandist for All For  One meanwhile Coda thinks back to a time  in the past when the class 1a students  hung out together inside their dorm we  learned that Shoji was in fact  comfortable with taking off his mask in  front of his classmates and he was also  comfortable telling them about his  tragic backstory Shoji's parents didn't  have the kind of arms that he was born  with he was the only one and because  they lived in a small Backwater Village  he faced a lot of discrimination and  abuse his unique physical features were  seen as a sign of quote unquote impure  blood whatever that means and he was  badly hurt and brutally scarred by these  bullies back then Shoji did explain to  his fellow mutant type Quirk users like  Koda and tokoyami that their experience  is different from his because they came  from cities there are still places out  there where people would go so far as to  eliminate heteromorph children in the  name of some misguided idea of Purity  Shoji's classmates are visibly upset  when they learn about all the hardships  that he had to go through and minata  apologizes for calling Shoji an octopus  earlier on in the story but Shoji says  it's all good he even chose tentacle as  his hero name and he enjoys stuff like  the most villain looking Hero rankings  so Shoji doesn't take himself or his  appear parents too seriously he doesn't  see himself as a victim and he is just  an incredibly strong and impressive  person the fact that he is a heteromorph  and the scars that he carries with him  have given Shoji a very specific Mission  and that mission is to become a Great  Hero and help his fellow mutant type  Quirk users while also proving to the  world that heteromorphs can be amazing  