tion away from the three massive  battles that are currently raging in  order to spend time on this and that got  me thinking there could be a bigger  reason why this exact topic is being  explored so extensively right now at the  end of the story it could be connected  to the last big mystery that mha still  hasn't revealed even though horikoshi  said that it would be revealed by the  end and I am of course referring to the  true identity of deku's Father since the  very beginning we've all been wondering  who deku's father is and why he's never  around even though he is apparently  alive and well and even though he and  inko are apparently still married Deku  and his mother don't seem to have any  sort of active relationship with deku's  Dad at least from what we've been able  to see based on what horikoshi has shown  us we know that deku's Dad has a fire  breathing Quirk and that he apparently  works abroad but that's about it but  what if the mysterious Hisashi midorias  fire breathing Quirk is not just a fire  breathing Quirk what if he actually has  a mutant type Quirk that turns his  entire body either fiery or extremely  hot and this makes him dangerous to be  around maybe his Quirk started out as  fire breathing but then it awakened or  revolved over time or maybe inko just  didn't tell us the full story but if  deku's Dad had a mutant type Quirk that  cannot be turned off and that could make  him a danger to the people around him  because of the fiery properties of his  Quirk then that would actually explain  why he has been absent from Deku and  inko's life he says she may believe that  staying as far away from his family as  possible is the best thing for them this  could be because he doesn't want them to  face discrimination due to the fact that  he is a heteromorph or it could be  because the true nature of his Quirk  makes him actually dangerous to be  around or it could be a combination of  those two factors honestly an  explanation along these lines is one of  the very few explanations that would  actually make sense why would a father  stay away from his family for years and  yet the family doesn't feel that he  abandoned them and they don't have any  animosity towards him it could be  because he is staying away for their own  safety and they might be aware of that  the CIA seen from the previous chapter  where someone who looks a lot like all  for one from behind is attacking and  murdering heteromorphs could also play a  part in this all for one may have a  connection to deku's father and so once  deku's father does make his appearance  it will be directly connected to the  final battle against all for one it's  hard to say what exactly that connection  would be and there are a lot of people  who believe that all for one is in fact  deku's dad but there are other  intriguing possibilities like deku's  father being one of the heteromorphs  whom all for one tried to kill or deku's  father approaching all for one for a  favor after Deku was born for example if  we accept that Hisashi has a quirk that  could make him a danger to others and if  Deku was born with that same type of  work then perhaps Hisashi approached all  for one anujiko in order to somehow  remove deku's Quirk before it evolved  into something dangerous so Deku may  have been born with a quirk but it was  taken from him for his own safety but in  order to get the Quirk removed deku's  father was forced to make a deal with  the devil and now he has to keep his  distance partially because of his own  Quirk and partially because of the  dangerous deal that he made with the  villains this is all speculation of  course but it's definitely intriguing to  speculate about deku's Father's true  identity I mean for all we know if he  really is a heteromorph he might have  already been shown on screen at some  point in the manga but we just didn't  recognize him definitely let me know  down in the comments who you think  deku's father is and why do you 